# Presentation-golden corpus manifest (the fanned-out bk2 set).
#
# presentation-corpus.sh captures, for each bk2, a canonical leg (VBL-keyed) and
# an intermediate leg (deterministic alpha=0.5) on the native -vk path under
# llvmpipe, at 16:9, across both LOD modes. See
# notes/plans/openpete-presentation-golden.md.
#
# Fields (pipe-separated):
#   name      bk2 basename under games/spyro-1/bk2/ (its .args sidecar is
#             auto-spliced by the binary, so --skip-to-level etc. need not be
#             repeated here; the corpus overrides aspect/LOD explicitly)
#   start     first VBL frame to sample: the first frame %interval==0 AFTER the
#             level finishes loading + the fade settles. Every row here is a
#             --skip-to-level movie, and those all settle by ~f1700 (the level
#             loads ~f1197, GS_Playing ~f1584, fade clears by ~f1650), so 1700 is
#             the shared start. A slower-loading scene overrides it per row.
#   interval  optional base VBL spacing (default 100).
#   freeze    optional 4th field: any non-empty value (e.g. "freeze") enables
#             --screenshot-freeze-backdrop for this row — needed for bk2s that
#             reach a pause / flight-results / level-exit state so the green
#             frozen-world backdrop is captured instead of a dark clear. Renders
#             an extra frame per present, so set it ONLY on freeze-reaching bk2s.
#
# The frame-limit and both sample grids are DERIVED from the bk2's own length (the
# input-frame count in its Input Log.txt). The base grid steps by `interval` from
# `start`, extended one point past the movie end; it is then subsampled to at most
# OPENPETE_MAX_SAMPLES (default 5) EVENLY-SPACED canonical frames so the golden
# stays broad across bk2s without a dense per-bk2 grid. The intermediate leg
# mirrors the kept canonical frames + interval/2.
#
# This is the Category-A fan-out: every --skip-to-level bk2 whose movie is long
# enough for the shared 1700 start (movie > 1800 frames). UI-only / cutscene /
# demo / TAS bk2s that need a bespoke start are tracked separately (plan §fan-out).
#
# name                                     | start | interval
alban-rescue                             | 1700
artisans-balloonist                      | 1700  | 100 | freeze
